/*
RMSTEST_34 - WHICH zones does set_zone_by_team give un-teamed players
preview-design.md Sec.15 item 14, second attempt

WHY THIS EXISTS - RMSTEST_29 DID NOT SETTLE IT
RMSTEST_29 ran three times at 8 players all un-teamed and returned eight
separate, evenly sized, ring-spaced GRASS patches every time. That was read as
confirming Sec.6.1's pinned choice. It does not. TWO hypotheses predict eight
separate patches and RMSTEST_29 cannot tell them apart:

  A  PINNED CHOICE. An un-teamed player keeps their own default player zone,
     playerNumber - 10. Player 1 is in -9, player 8 in -2. Occupied set -9..-2.
  B  Every player carries an engine-internal TeamNumber even when solo, so the
     zone is TeamNumber - 9 exactly as guide:1056 says, with no special case.
     Player 1 is in -8, player 8 in -1. Occupied set -8..-1.

Both give eight DISTINCT zones, so both give eight non-touching lands. What
RMSTEST_29 did rule out - and this part stands - is the third reading, that
un-teamed collapses to a single shared zone and the lands merge.

Note B is not in conflict with a team of one failing to register in
TEAMn_SIZEm / PLAYERx_TEAMy. Those labels are about what the LOBBY reports;
a zone is an internal land-growth property. The two can disagree and B is the
hypothesis that they do.

METHOD
The hypotheses differ only in WHICH absolute zones are occupied, so probe the
two boundary zones that separate them. Plant neutral lands with an explicit
zone and measure whether each may touch the player lands:

  DIRT   zone -9   nobody's zone under B, player 1's under A
  DESERT zone -1   nobody's zone under A, player 8's under B
  DIRT3  zone  5   nobody's zone under EITHER - the instrument control

other_zone_avoidance_distance 20 is the instrument, exactly as in RMSTEST_29:
lands in different zones are pushed 20 apart, lands sharing a zone are not.
No player identification is needed, which matters because a random-map export
carries no player-owned units - every unit belongs to gaia - so there is no way
to tell player 1's land from player 8's. Terrain type carries the signal
instead.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches GRASS
  plus a minimum-distance calculation from each probe terrain to GRASS.
  The reading is WHICH probe comes within 20 tiles of any GRASS tile.

PREDICTIONS, RECORDED BEFORE THE RUN
1. Under A: DIRT gets close to GRASS (min distance well under 20, plausibly
   touching); DESERT stays at or above 20. Sec.6.1's pinned choice is measured
   and stands.
2. Under B: DESERT gets close; DIRT stays at or above 20. Sec.6.1 changes to
   "an un-teamed player's zone is TeamNumber - 9 like everyone else", the
   special case disappears, and the model gets simpler.
3. DIRT3 must stay at or above 20 in every run. IT IS THE CONTROL AND IT IS NOT
   OPTIONAL - if the control comes in close, other_zone_avoidance_distance is
   not doing anything here and NEITHER probe can be read. This is the check
   RMSTEST_29 lacked, which is why RMSTEST_29's result was over-read.
4. If BOTH probes stay at or above 20 across all runs, the result is
   inconclusive rather than negative: the same-zone probe has to get near a
   player land by chance, and nothing forces it to. Re-run with larger neutral
   lands before concluding anything.

Note the asymmetry in strength. "Stays 20 away" is ENFORCED by the avoidance
rule, so it is a strong signal. "Comes close" merely means it was ALLOWED to,
so it depends on the draw - which is why three runs, and why prediction 4
exists.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200) WITH 8 PLAYERS, ALL PLAYERS UN-TEAMED (plain FFA,
no team setup at all - this is the default in the scenario editor and needs no
lobby). RUN IT THREE TIMES.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain SNOW

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    number_of_tiles 300
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    set_zone_by_team
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* probe A - player 1's DEFAULT player zone under hypothesis A */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DIRT
    number_of_tiles 1500
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    zone -9
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* probe B - player 8's TEAM zone under hypothesis B */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DESERT
    number_of_tiles 1500
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    zone -1
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

  /* CONTROL - nobody's zone under either hypothesis. Must stay 20 away. */
  create_land
  {
    terrain_type DIRT3
    number_of_tiles 1500
    base_size 5
    clumping_factor 20
    border_fuzziness 0
    zone 5
    other_zone_avoidance_distance 20
  }

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>

/* NO <CLIFF_GENERATION> HEADER. An empty one generates cliffs, which is how the
   2026-08-01 batch contaminated itself. Cliffs would put terrain 16 under
   themselves (guide:1325) and add a second thing moving terrain around. */

<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>
